-### 5. Derivative propagation and declassification
+### 5. Meeting action items and explicit task promotion
+
+An automatically extracted action item is a meeting-owned record. Extraction,
+meeting finalization, agent runs, providers, and background jobs may create or
+update that meeting record, but must never directly create a Product-Suite task
+or work item.
+
+An authorized meeting member may explicitly promote an action item. Promotion
+uses the existing proposal/apply boundary as a user-visible approval step:
+
+1. The proposal remains conversation-scoped and references the source meeting,
+   source action item, and access conversation.
+2. The approval command is initiated by the authenticated user; the proposal,
+   model, provider, or extractor cannot set `approvedBy` or bypass confirmation.
+3. The created task/work item records immutable links to the source meeting,
+   action item, proposal, and access conversation.
+4. Supported suggested owner, due/start date, parent, and dependencies are
+   carried forward with their source evidence. A suggestion becomes a canonical
+   assignment/reference only when it resolves to an existing same-tenant entity
+   and the approving user confirms it.
+5. Missing or uncertain values remain `null`/unassigned. Do not substitute the
+   approver, current date, root project, or an empty dependency set as if those
+   were extracted facts. Unresolved suggestions may remain visible as scoped
+   proposal metadata for user correction, but are not written into canonical
+   task fields.
+
+The post-meeting surface is a compact candidate card, not a field form. Its
+default state shows only a plain-language title, one-line reason/source, and the
+recommended next step. The actions are:
+
+- **Add:** explicit approval of the currently displayed candidate version. It
+  creates exactly one task/work item using only confirmed, resolvable values.
+- **Adjust:** opens an inline comment/conversation with the agent. The agent may
+  offer at most two or three natural-language choices: `simple task`, `planned
+  work item`, or `keep as meeting follow-up`. It returns a new immutable/versioned
+  candidate for approval; it does not mutate prior versions or create work.
+- **Dismiss:** records the user's decision and creates no task/work item.
+
+Owner/date/parent/dependencies and provenance remain available underneath the
+card through progressive disclosure, and appear by default only when a value is
+material to the recommendation, unresolved, or explicitly requested. Adjust
+cannot fabricate a structured value; uncertainty remains visible and unset.
+The adjustment comment and agent response use the existing product-owned
+collaboration/run protocol, reference the candidate version, and execute inside
+the meeting access conversation. They do not create a new identity or chat
+authority.
+
+Normal task creation preserves the meeting conversation scope and remains
+available only to authorized members unless the user takes the separate
+declassification action below.
+
+### 6. Derivative propagation and declassification
 
 Meeting proposal ingest reads only meetings visible to the initiating caller
-and stamps the source access conversation on the proposal. Proposal list,
-detail, accept, reject, and audit paths repeat the current-membership check.
+and stamps the source action item and access conversation on the proposal.
