+## Delivery as a medium-PR train
+
+The security boundary is one design, delivered as three independently
+reviewable medium PRs. Each PR must merge before the next begins so no parallel
+branch independently edits the shared schema, authorization, or tool files.
+
+### PR A - Authority foundation
+
+Lock the cross-domain contract, add the additive schema/backfill, and implement
+the server-derived current-membership primitive. This PR must not enable a new
+content read or meeting-search surface. Existing missing origins deny.
+
+### PR B - Provenance and enforcement
+
+Propagate the access origin through meetings, derivatives, proposals, and
+explicit task promotion; then enforce caller scope on every existing direct and
+indirect read/action path. This is the activation PR for the authority boundary,
+including the rule that automatic action items remain meeting-owned.
+The same PR owns the compact `Add`/`Adjust`/`Dismiss` candidate-review flow so
+the UI cannot race ahead of the authority and promotion semantics.
+
+### PR C - Bounded meeting search and conformance
+
+Add summary/action-item-only `search_meetings` to the product-owned run protocol
+and prove the full matrix against a real database. Raw transcript retrieval
+remains deferred and is not a hidden fallback.
+
+Each PR has its own RED/GREEN evidence, migration/rebase check, security review,
+and exact-head CI gate. Do not combine the train into one oversized PR.
+
 ## Migration and legacy data
 
 1. Add nullable columns and same-tenant indexes/references without changing
    read behavior.
+   This includes work-item access/source columns and the minimum immutable
+   candidate-revision representation required by `Adjust`.
 2. Create one conversation for each existing meeting and grant only its
    verified owner an admin membership. Do not translate legacy `team` or
    `public` values into tenant-wide grants.
